# Every VITE_* value below is public (inlined into the bundle) and validated by
# src/lib/runtimeConfig.js: a malformed value fails `npm run build`. The values
# are commented out, so a straight copy builds with every optional feature off;
# uncomment and fill in only what you use.
#
# Supabase — powers blog view counts. Leave unset to disable the feature entirely
# (the site falls back to no counts and still builds/runs normally).
#
# Create a free project at https://supabase.com, then copy these from
# Project Settings → API. The anon key is a public key and is safe to ship in the
# client bundle; Row Level Security protects the database (see documentation/data.md).
# Use the publishable (sb_publishable_…) or legacy anon key, never a secret key.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your-key

# Analytics — privacy-friendly GoatCounter (no cookies / consent banner).
# Create a free site at https://www.goatcounter.com and set this to your code
# (the "<code>" in https://<code>.goatcounter.com). Leave unset to disable.
# VITE_GOATCOUNTER_CODE=your-goatcounter-code

# Contact form — optional Formspree endpoint override. Leave unset to use the
# site's default form (see src/hooks/useContactForm.js).
# VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/your-form-id
